% =============================================================================
% references.bib: bibliography database, read by biber through biblatex
% (set up in preamble/references.tex).
%
% HOW THIS FILE WORKS
% - Each entry is @type{key, field = {value}, ...}. Cite it in the text with
%   \cite{key}; the key is the only thing the text needs to know.
% - Only entries you actually cite are printed, so it is safe to keep every
%   source here. The IEEE style numbers them in order of first citation.
% - Keys follow  firstauthorsurname + year + first title word  (all lower
%   case), e.g. kumar2018rev2. Entries are in alphabetical order of key.
% - Write authors as "Surname, Given Names" joined by "and". biblatex-ieee
%   abbreviates given names to initials and switches to "et al." itself.
% - Titles keep the capitalisation of the source; wrap acronyms and proper
%   nouns in braces ({REV2}, {MCP}) so no style can ever lower-case them.
% - date = {YYYY-MM} or {YYYY}. eid = article number ("Art. no." in IEEE).
% - Journal and proceedings names use IEEE abbreviations, as in the
%   literature notes.
% - arXiv preprints are @misc with eprinttype = {arxiv}; they print as
%   "arXiv:2508.20829 [cs.LG]".
%
% SOURCES
% Built from the exports in citations/ (EndNote .enw, .ris, .bib), with
% authors, venues, volumes and pages cross-checked against Crossref (all
% DOIs) and the arXiv API (all preprints) on 2026-09-29. Where the export
% and a literature note disagreed, the Crossref record was used; notes on
% those entries say so.
% =============================================================================


